Today was less about AI and more about clarity.

Over the last few weeks I've been refining the identity behind Project Ocean.

Not adding more features.
Not making bigger promises.

Just asking a simple question:

What should AI actually become?

The answer keeps bringing me back to the same idea:

AI that remembers you.

Not just information.
Not just prompts.

Context.
Continuity.
Trust.

We're still early, still building, and still learning.

But every step forward makes the vision a little clearer.

The future of AI won't be defined only by intelligence.

It will be defined by the quality of the relationship between humans and the systems they choose to trust.

